{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>\"I, being on the way, HaShem guided me to the house of my master's brother.\"</b> It is possible to interpret that this verse alludes to the fact that the earth was contracted for him, according to the view of our Rabbis of blessed memory, as if he said: I was going along this great road — this is what he means by ״I, being on the way, HaShem guided me״ — and I was at the beginning of the road and found myself at the house of my master's brother. And this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: ״ואבא היום אל העין״ — ״theיום I set out and theיום I arrived.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:45.912599521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}